      "field": "principle",
      "text": "For thus saith the LORD of hosts; Yet once, it is a little while, and I will shake the heavens, and the earth... and the desire of all nations shall come: and I will fill this house with glory. The second temple's glory exceeded Solomon's because the Desire Himself walked its courts. First principle: God's greatest glory in a place arrives quietly, in a Person.",
